  "notes": [
    "The earlier 60-record catalogue epoch is retained in validation-pre-domestic-iraq.json; the prior 98-record pre-sensitivity epoch is retained separately.",
    "The 31,989 physical scopes are covered by 7,042 sourcing requirement groups in the roll-up packet; only 137 groups were evaluated and 6,905 remain pending.",
    "The fabrication screens are candidate-context-linked but are not mapped to railway purchasing quantities or occurrences.",
    "The reported 8 October 2026 Kurdistan Region bulk-cement observation remains separate from the CSO national cement series and is not treated as a Baghdad installed rate.",
    "Eight domestic supplier/manufacturing leads cover state cement production, steel fabrication, reinforcing steel, GRP pipe, a not-yet-confirmed aluminium extrusion project, GRP façade fabrication, polymer raw materials and epoxy/polyester supply; none is a quotation or qualified component.",
    "All five current sourcing publications were regenerated from the expanded 273-record offline source seed and passed semantic replay against sealed inputs and source snapshots.",
    "Three concrete batch cost screens add source-linked materials, declared labour-hour scenarios and 20% uplift; they remain generic planning recipes without measured mix yields, process hours or candidate-takeoff mapping.",
    "The candidate material takeoff still preserves 27,216 located occurrences across 2,269 manufacturing groups and 4,773 unlocated accounts; no railway group declares labour hours, so no candidate-level fabrication uplift is applied.",
    "Three new Iraq-local composites supplier/fabricator leads were added: NUBIN GRP/GFRP façade fabrication, Abr AlQamar polyester/epoxy supply, and Al-Mniee polymer raw materials. These are candidate RFQ leads; no exact glass-fibre product, compatible price, rail-body qualification or factory capacity is established.",
    "The GFRP local-fabrication estimate applies an explicit 8/16/32 skilled-hour sensitivity per 10 m² to listed UK cloth/resin material extensions, converts GBP at the dated CBI reference, then applies 20% to known material plus CSO base wage. Core and adhesive remain unpriced/unresolved, and tooling, consumables, import charges, QA, fire/smoke and process qualification are outside the partial amount.",
    "Hierarchy-only procurement cross-references associate 4,766 of 4,773 unlocated accounts with related car, bogie, secondary, span or bank quote scopes; these 230 links are non-additive context only, with no package quantity, mass or cost allocation. Seven network-level infrastructure obligations remain unlinked."
  ],
